# data file for fldtk fluid (Fast Light User Interface Designer)
version 1.0000
comment {Assign the fldtk Fluid editor's own icon at runtime.

Ported from FLTK's fluid/fluid_icon.fl -- see that file's own
comment for the "run fluid on itself, pick a PNG, write code" authoring
workflow this project doesn't need (the embedded pixmaps/fluid-icon.png
below is a fixed, already-decided asset, re-encoded non-interlaced from
FLTK's own fluid-128.png -- fl.png_image.PngImage doesn't support
Adam7 interlacing yet, a documented gap; pixel content is identical,
confirmed via a PIL byte-for-byte comparison during conversion).
}
  {
    in_source
    in_header
  }
data fluidIconData
  {
    private
    local
    filename {pixmaps/fluid-icon.png}
  }
Function {makeFluidIcon(Window win)}
  {
  }
  {
    code {auto icon = new PngImage(null, fluidIconData);
if (!icon.fail()) \{
    win.icon(icon);
\}}
      {
      }
  }
